hey guys it's joanna here for those of  you who are back in the gym  here is a total body strength and  conditioning workout  this workout will help you to build lean  muscles and  to burn fat so there will be a total of  four  supersets targeting every major muscle  in the body we will be doing two  exercises  back to back without any rest in between  and we want to aim for  four sets okay you want to make sure  that you're lifting  heavy enough to only perform 12 to 15  reps  per set if you can do more reps then  you have to lift heavier let's start  the first episode will be targeting your  legs thighs  glutes as well as your shoulders goblet  squat  and sumo squat single arm press so have  two dumbbells ready one heavy and one  lighter let's start with goblet squat  stance shoulder width apart with your  toes pointed forward  and lift the heavy dumbbell directly in  front of you  push your butt back and squat as low as  you can if you can  try to get your elbows to tap your  thighs and push back  up with your heels push your butt back  engage your core  and keep your body upright  [Music]  once you've completed 12 to 15  repetitions  let's move on to the next workout  [Music]  step wide with your toes pointed out in  a sumo squat position  so we want to be working on your inner  thighs as well as your shoulders  grab the light dumbbell and as you come  up  press the dumbbell above your head lower  yourself back down  and up again so this workout will work  on your glutes  your inner thighs as well as your  shoulders  once you've completed the right arm  switch  and let's continue working on the left  arm  again remember to keep your body upright  so do not  hunch push your butt back and engage  your core throughout  the workout use the strength from your  legs to help you drive  the dumbbell up and you should feel the  work on your shoulders as well  [Music]  well done that is the end of one set  take a short break  and repeat another three more sets  before moving on to the second superset  the second superset will be targeting  your back muscles  traps as well as your shoulders bent  over barbell row  and barbell upright row so for this  super set you will need  two barbells one heavy weight between  15 to 30 kilos and one light weight  between 10 to 15 kilos let's start with  the first workout bend over barbell roll  you will need the heavy barbell for this  workout  so hold the barbell in a reverse grip  position  with your palms facing up push your butt  back  and bend slightly at your hips keeping  your back flat  and chest lifted pull the bar towards  your core  and point your elbows back so do not  spread your elbows out  feel the contraction on your back  muscles before releasing the barbell to  the starting position  and remember to keep your knees soft so  do not lock your knees  this is one of my favorite workouts to  build strength and size  for your back once you've completed all  your wraps  let's immediately move into barbell  upright roll  this workout is really great to target  your shoulders as well as your upper  back  hold the barbell at shoulder width apart  with your palms facing your body  stand upright and pull the barbell up  with your elbows pointed out  just below your chest level lift the  barbell straight up towards  your chest with the elbows pointed out  and  keeping the barbell close to your body  remember to stand tall  brace your core and keep your back  straight with your chest up throughout  the workout  and remember that your arms should not  go higher than your shoulders  so it should just be at about chest  level pause at the top and slowly lower  the barbell down  and again pull it up pause and  lower the barbell down brace your core  keep your body  upright chest lifted throughout the  workout and avoid using momentum to lift  the barbell  up so we want to do at least 12 to 15  repetitions  and that's one set complete another two  to three more sets  before moving on to the third superset  the next superset will be working on  your chest as well as your triceps  alternating dumbbell press and narrow  push-ups  you'll need a bench and one pair of  medium weight dumbbells between 5 to 8  kilos each  so let's start with alternating dumbbell  press lie face up on a flat bench with  your feet  firmly planted on the floor spread your  elbows out and lower the dumbbells to a  90 degree angle  this is your starting position press the  right dumbbell  up toward the ceiling by flexing and  engaging your chest muscle  lower it back down and alternate with  the left dumbbell  so keep alternating between hands you  should feel the engagement on your chest  muscles to engage your chest the  dumbbells should always maintain a chest  level so don't lift it too high by  alternating the presses  this will increase and maintain the  tension on the lowered  arm once you have completed 12  repetitions on each side  drop the dumbbells and get down onto the  floor  for narrow push-ups for narrow push-ups  you want to keep your arms close to your  body with your elbows pointed back  lower yourself down and push up using  the strength  from your triceps this is a more  challenging workout  so let's keep it to 10 to 12 repetitions  if you're struggling to do the full  push-up then drop onto your knees  remember to engage your core and keep  your back flat  do not arch your lower back your upper  body should be feeling  really tired by now take a short break  and complete another  two to three more sets and let's move  into the final super set  it's going to be a total body movement  focusing  on your core kettlebell swing and plank  if you have a kettlebell then grab one  that weighs between 8 to 16 kilos  if not you can also replace this with a  dumbbell  stand slightly wider than shoulder width  apart with the kettlebell  in the middle hold the kettlebell with  both arms  you want to keep a slight bend at the  knees  slowly lower the kettlebells back  between your legs to create momentum  use the power from your hips and core  drive your hips forward and straighten  your back to bring the kettlebell  up to shoulder level let the kettlebell  return  between your legs and repeat the  movement remember that  the power should be coming from your  hips and your core  not your upper body so your arms should  only be helping you to hold on to the  kettlebell  this is a great explosive movement to  not only work on your core  but to work on your total body in  increasing your heart rate and burn  fat i love to do this workout as my  finisher exercise  once you've completed all your wraps get  down  onto the floor into a plank brace your  core  keep your back flat and maintain this  plank position  do not arch your lower back or pipe your  butt up hold the plank  for 40 seconds and in the final 20  seconds  let's rock forward and back  so that's going to challenge your core  even more  only 20 seconds  [Music]  and you're done take a short break  stretch if you need to  and complete another two to three more  sets  before you end your workout you got this  supersets are a great technique for  those of you who are tight on time  this workout will hit all the major  muscles in  under one hour so try this workout  and you can even do it at home if you  have dumbbells and barbells  if you enjoy this workout if you want  more gym workouts then let me know in  the comments below  hit the like button share this video on  save this video and do subscribe to my  youtube channel check out a lot more  home workout videos gym workouts recipes  and nutritional tips  on my youtube channel and i will see you  next time stay safe  all the best
 

